WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.004
WEF Institutional Corridor.

00:00:02.954 --> 00:00:13.386
A systematic mapping of the convergence between World Economic Forum governance, G7 central banking policy, and Canadian federal fiscal architecture during the period of MAID Track Two expansion.

00:00:13.386 --> 00:00:15.034
Key figures.

00:00:15.034 --> 00:00:19.125
Three central bank governors connected through the World Economic Forum.

00:00:19.125 --> 00:00:29.249
Chrystia Freeland served as WEF Board of Trustees member from 2019 to 2024, concurrent with her role as Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Finance.

00:00:29.249 --> 00:00:31.556
The institutional corridor.

00:00:31.556 --> 00:00:40.761
How the World Economic Forum connects three central banking positions to Canadian domestic policy through overlapping board memberships, policy frameworks, and fiscal architecture.

00:00:40.761 --> 00:00:42.488
Chrystia Freeland.

00:00:42.488 --> 00:00:47.613
WEF Board of Trustees member from 2019 to 2024.

00:00:47.613 --> 00:00:57.829
Simultaneously served as Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Finance, with direct authority over federal fiscal policy during MAID Track Two expansion and pandemic emergency spending.

00:00:57.829 --> 00:01:01.068
Christine Lagarde and the European Central Bank.

00:01:01.068 --> 00:01:04.340
ECB President since 2019.

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:14.181
The Millennial Falcon tracking system identifies a direct institutional corridor linking ECB quantitative easing policy to coordinated G7 fiscal expansion frameworks.

00:01:14.181 --> 00:01:16.193
The convergence network.

00:01:16.193 --> 00:01:21.204
A table showing the overlapping institutional connections between all five mapped nodes.

00:01:21.204 --> 00:01:23.568
Canada Infrastructure Bank.

00:01:23.568 --> 00:01:25.988
The fiscal deployment mechanism.

00:01:25.988 --> 00:01:28.931
35 billion dollar federal mandate.

00:01:28.931 --> 00:01:31.159
CEO Tamara Vrooman.

00:01:31.159 --> 00:01:37.170
The CIB is the exact instrument through which the Brookfield Maple Fund thesis becomes operational policy.

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:43.727
It co-invests federal capital alongside private asset managers in infrastructure, clean energy, and transit.

00:01:43.727 --> 00:01:45.886
The asset convergence.

00:01:45.886 --> 00:01:48.181
BlackRock and Larry Fink.

00:01:48.181 --> 00:01:53.602
The world's largest asset manager holds 308 million dollars in Brookfield shares.

00:01:53.602 --> 00:02:00.056
A 1,373 percent increase filed with the SEC in November 2025.

00:02:00.056 --> 00:02:04.159
Fink and Carney served together on the WEF Board of Trustees.

00:02:04.159 --> 00:02:08.795
Fink became WEF interim co-chair in August 2025.

00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:13.329
Combined assets under management: 14.5 trillion dollars.

00:02:13.329 --> 00:02:16.909
BlackRock's ESG mandates create the demand.

00:02:16.909 --> 00:02:19.988
Brookfield supplies the green infrastructure.

00:02:19.988 --> 00:02:22.897
The CIB funds it with federal capital.

00:02:22.897 --> 00:02:24.590
One network.

00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:26.306
One thesis.

00:02:26.306 --> 00:02:28.522
One corridor of capital.
